<title>USA: Western Transmedia finalizes terms.</title>
<headline>Western Transmedia finalizes terms.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Transmedia Co Inc said it will eliminate the 800,000 Transmedia Network Inc warrants exercisable at $15 per share proposed to be issued as part of sale to Transmedia Network.</p>
<p>Further terms were unavailable. It said it was finalizing terms for the previously announced sale of its franchise covering California, Oregon, Washington and parts of Nevada to Transmedia Network Inc.</p>
<p>Shareholders will vote on the deal at a special meeting in late-December 1996 or early January 1997. Upon closing, Western Transmedia's total cash will approximate $9 million.</p>
</text>
